n":{"commit_sha":"4b54fbd6e0854750d7795877876ab81957690ff1","position":"1787210442466002001-ea1cb208-9c02-45c1-9eac-6335498aff9a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6a854167d17ce5a335d11751567044a870adff03bf86cc92a3d813511dfbcd5a","event_uuid":"4132a070-565f-4934-a82e-fa9196b8463c","position":{"commit_sha":"5da0d0a5104426442603ea35944e1158d68166b5","position":"1787219528831971001-4132a070-565f-4934-a82e-fa9196b8463c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-236_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"d76562af-5785-4ef5-899c-57d3a1e383f5","comments":[],"created_at":1787185966335615001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dced7568-e0e3-4230-be66-829be735b1a3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"3726-a1b0-c9bb-4d83"},{"link_uuid":"8bd59efe-e0b2-46d0-8fa4-84adbff3e3d2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ed5e-bcfc-5c73-42ea"},{"link_uuid":"749efb05-d63d-4129-b9fa-2ae6a125a440","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"231b-a54a-549d-4fc6"},{"link_uuid":"efddb57b-65ec-4029-922e-2f846b578a8a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e641-022d-fb1e-4df1"},{"link_uuid":"af748872-1c3f-463e-a233-cc522815f3ba","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1110-7c98-eed3-4179"}],"description":"## What\n\nCut the emit-side surfaces over to `[non-codebase]`, teaching the recognition-side surfaces to\naccept the legacy spelling without documenting it.\n\nCUTOVER (emit): `plan_review_E2.md:12`, `plan_review_E6.md:12`, `plan_review_F1.md:10`,\n`coach_moves.py` move 14 (comment + template).\nCOMPATIBILITY (recognize both): `completion_verifier.md`, `plan_review_evidence_kind.md`,\n`plan_review_ac_process_gate.md`, `.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-measurement-provenance.md`\n(its SCOPE clause gates whether the criterion applies at all), the eval-spec fixtures.\n\n## Verbatim quoters of the move-14 template\n\n`coach_moves.py` move 14's template string is reproduced VERBATIM in two other places. Changing\nthe template without them leaves the docs misquoting real coach output:\n\n- `docs/plan-review-gate.md:335` — the coach-move table row. IN SCOPE for this story. (No\n  automated byte-identity gate enforces this row — the nearby guide parity test covers overlay\n  ranges, not the move table — so it is a doc-accuracy defect rather than a CI break, and it is\n  fixed here because this story owns the template.)\n- `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md:204` — OUT OF SCOPE, owned by S5, which also\n  flips the coupled assertion in `tests/unit/test_guides.py:76-82`. S5 `depends_on` this story,\n  so the two land in order and the whole stack lands together; the guide's quote is stale only\n  within the stack, never on `main`.\n\n## Boundary with S7 in `completion_verifier.md`\n\nBoth stories edit that file and S7 `depends_on` this one, so the edits are ordered. The split is\nby concern: THIS story makes the file RECOGNIZE both TAG spellings. The `kind` WIRE-VALUE emit\ncutover ADR 0101 requires \"in lockstep\" — including `completion_verifier.md:224`\n(`kind`: `codebase-verifiable` or `operator-attested`) — is explicitly S7's, alongside\n`contracts.py` and the JSON schema, so the emitted enum changes in ONE place rather than being\nsplit across two changes.\n\n## Why this is ONE commit\n\nThree gates are coupled to this text and all fail if split:\n1. `tests/unit/test_measurement_provenance_criterion.py` pins SHA256 digests AND exact line\n   counts for five files. Its `_contract_lines()` selector keeps lines containing\n   `\"OPERATOR-ATTESTED RULE\"` or `\"[operator-attested]\"` — cut over without widening the\n   SELECTOR and it matches ZERO lines, failing with a misleading\n   \"expected 1 contract line(s), found 0\".\n2. `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` is generated from these prompts and gated by\n   `registry.validate_criteria_guide(...) == []` in five test files plus content pins in\n   `tests/unit/test_generated_surface_markers.py`.\n3. The `reviewers/index.json` drift gate fires on any front-matter change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Emit-side prompts and coach move 14 instruct `[non-codebase]`.\n- [x] Recognition-side prompts state that the legacy spelling is still accepted.\n- [x] `_contract_lines()` selects the new text; digests and counts are recomputed in this commit.\n- [x] `python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide` run and committed;\n      `validate_criteria_guide` returns `[]`.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_E2.md","reason":"emit-side cutover to [non-codebase]"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_E6.md","reason":"emit-side cutover to [non-codebase]"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_F1.md","reason":"emit-side cutover to [non-codebase]"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/coach_moves.py","reason":"move 14 comment and template"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"coach-move table row quotes the move-14 template verbatim"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md","reason":"recognize both tag spellings (kind emit stays S7)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_evidence_kind.md","reason":"recognize both tag spellings"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json","reason":"both tag-bearing checklist rules at :1241 and :1245"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md","reason":"regenerated from the prompts"},{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/criterion-pins.json","reason":"guide digest manifest, regenerated after the guide changed"},{"path":"src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md","reason":"author guide cutover absorbed from S5 (served verbatim by rebar explain plan)"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_guides.py","reason":"flip the documented-tag assertion and add the undocumented-alias negative test"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_measurement_provenance_criterion.py","reason":"widen the _contract_lines selector and recompute the contract digests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_s4_prompt_cutover.py","reason":"emit-side cutover happy path"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_s4_prompt_cutover_edge.py","reason":"held-out edge oracle: verbatim doc quote, both registry rules, digest recompute, selector trap"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","3726-a1b0-c9bb-4d83"],["parent","6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30"],["relates_to","1110-7c98-eed3-4179"],["relates_to","e641-022d-fb1e-4df1"],["relates_to","ed5e-bcfc-5c73-42ea"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6f5a-4a49-7bbf-4a30","parent_status_uuid":"4b865360-1740-4df3-aa2d-1218d78ee7f4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f371-ca39-181c-4091","ticket_type":"story","title":"S4 — cut prompts, coach text and the generated guide over to [non-codebase]","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a89ca025-379f-4a7b-9595-de874e72c2fe","9a6e2191-6d00-4798-bf34-2092e3553d2d","1c8f231c-f7c2-43ef-a4f5-c3f1876dde97","c285d174-47c7-4bd9-b5f5-00eee340ca4c","1ee2d801-7d9e-4e4e-92c8-d99601989201","4b865360-1740-4df3-aa2d-1218d78ee7f4","1aa3fb99-e6bd-4241-aa9e-709b32346b84","8bd59efe-e0b2-46d0-8fa4-84adbff3e3d2","749efb05-d63d-4129-b9fa-2ae6a125a440","efddb57b-65ec-4029-922e-2f846b578a8a